  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported optimization applies without weakening coverage or adding risk. The workflow already satisfies the dependency-cache pattern (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE): both the test and lint jobs use ruby/setup-ruby with bundler-cache: true, so Ruby dependency downloads are already cached. The fail-fast pattern (P-LIT-FAIL-FAST) is contraindicated because the test job's matrix runs three Ruby versions (3.3, 3.4, 4.0) specifically to preserve cross-version test coverage; cancelling remaining matrix cells after one failure would drop required outcomes, matching the pattern's 'Every matrix outcome is required' contraindication. The custom-timeout pattern (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT) lacks a representative successful-duration baseline (CI history is marked not_a_measured_baseline / historical_context_only) and carries the 'Valid slow runs exceed the proposed limit' contraindication, so adding timeout-minutes risks false failures on valid slow runs such as the yard doc-generation job. Other patterns (stale-run cancellation, schedule suppression, test selection/prioritization) either target CI-service configuration outside workflow_yaml or would reduce required coverage.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT"]
}
